-	Different management techniques
  o	Waterfall model
    	Project is worked in a linear model where there’s a set path and steps that must be taken
    	Not flexible because cannot move back to prior steps if needed
    	Does not consult with the costumer as much either
  o	Agile model
    	Project is worked in iterations
    	Feedback is given on each iteration to the project is always up to date with the customer and checked
    	Can move back to previous aspects of the project and can jump around as needed


